untime-0.1.0.tgz</code><br/><code style="overflow-wrap:anywhere">b142f96cff445d66bfde00b2d18dfbfc9ab8952c475c8d973bc87d917acd3ce8</code></li><li><code>mcpcn-react-0.1.0.tgz</code><br/><code style="overflow-wrap:anywhere">11783d094966405567ba4525f019f03b17e5f5c19267074c2342849bbf07af5f</code></li><li><code>mcpcn-themes-0.1.0.tgz</code><br/><code style="overflow-wrap:anywhere">55b4fdcbfd5d9af07904e27e973b08fdad870aa3b74f252554f9ff031565a1c4</code></li><li><code>mcpcn-registry-0.1.0.tgz</code><br/><code style="overflow-wrap:anywhere">b2d087bcf5e74854102dba7c5fd9778f82dad32a86b3e96e92b2938293773bbf</code></li><li><code>mcpcn-0.1.0.tgz</code><br/><code style="overflow-wrap:anywhere">5845a6a4fd9477885fe49526a27dee4b86bf9fedb0124e46acd9db424c3e439a</code></li><li><code>mcpcn-server-0.1.0.tgz</code><br/><code style="overflow-wrap:anywhere">e30bdc80c9e0ad4c3abf4a1ab4ba482b0a9e73b634df434a531830babb415b6b</code></li></ul></details></div></section><p><a href="/create">Configure a different manager, theme, host or selection.</a> Both modes require an existing React application. JavaScript output is not supported by this source installer.</p><h2 id="provider">Mount your provider</h2><p>The generated <code>components/mcpcn<!-- -->/provider.tsx</code> applies your chosen theme and creates the selected adapter on the client. Mount <code>MCPCNProvider</code> around your MCP App UI. Import paths in these examples are relative to your project root; adjust them to the location of your integration file.</p><pre class="code">&quot;use client&quot;;

import { useEffect, useState, type ReactNode } from &quot;react&quot;;
import { AgentAppProvider, detectAdapter, type AgentAppAdapter } from &quot;./_mcpcn/runtime&quot;;
import &quot;./styles.css&quot;;

export function MCPCNProvider({ children }: { children: ReactNode }) {
  const [adapter, setAdapter] = useState&lt;AgentAppAdapter | null&gt;(null);
  useEffect(() =&gt; { setAdapter(detectAdapter()); }, []);
  return &lt;div className=&quot;mcpcn&quot; data-mcpcn-theme=&quot;default&quot;&gt;
    {adapter ? &lt;AgentAppProvider adapter={adapter}&gt;{children}&lt;/AgentAppProvider&gt;
      : &lt;p role=&quot;status&quot; aria-busy=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Preparing app connection…&lt;/p&gt;}
  &lt;/div&gt;;
}
</pre><p>Copy mode includes local styles. Package mode imports <code>@mcpcn/react/styles.css</code> and <code>@mcpcn/themes/default.css</code>. The provider sets <code>data-mcpcn-theme</code> for Default, Graphite or Violet.</p><h2 id="first-component">Your first component</h2><p>For this example, add <code>approval-card</code> using the configurator. Connect <code>onApprove</code> to your own authorized action, and provide its pending/error handling.</p><pre class="code">import { MCPCNProvider } from &quot;./components/mcpcn/provider&quot;;
import { ApprovalCard } from &quot;./components/mcpcn/approval-card&quot;;

export function ReviewAction({ onApprove }: { onApprove: () =&gt; void }) {
  return &lt;MCPCNProvider&gt;
    &lt;ApprovalCard
      title=&quot;Send this email?&quot;
      riskLevel=&quot;medium&quot;
      actionLabel=&quot;Send&quot;
      changes={[{ label: &quot;Recipients&quot;, after: &quot;43 customers&quot; }]}
      onAction={({ type }) =&gt; { if (type === &quot;approve&quot;) onApprove(); }}
    /&gt;
  &lt;/MCPCNProvider&gt;;
}</pre><h2 id="host-compatibility">Host compatibility</h2><p>Auto detect uses the existing runtime detection: OpenAI compatibility when that host surface exists, the official MCP Apps adapter inside an iframe, and a local mock otherwise. Standard MCP Apps explicitly selects <code>OfficialMCPAdapter</code>; OpenAI compatibility explicitly selects <code>OpenAIAdapter</code>. Configuration does not grant host capabilities or server permissions.</p><p>The configurator previews are authored local examples. Their actions never execute host tools or install files, and they are not a live host acceptance check.</p><h2 id="security-boundaries">Security boundaries</h2><p>A UI approval is not server authorization. Keep raw personal data in private UI or server state, send only deliberate context to the model, and validate every app-initiated tool call on the server. Treat tools, membership and destructive operations as application-owned permissions.</p><h2 id="registry">Registry</h2><p>The source registry contains component and workflow-block entries with their local source closure. Choose a registry you trust, review installed files, and retain the lockfile to detect changes before updating. The CLI reports required dependencies instead of running a package manager for you.</p><h2 id="server-helpers">Server helpers</h2><p>The separate <code>@mcpcn/server</code> helpers support MCP tool/resource registration. Client installation does not create a server, authorization policy or production endpoint. Connect your reviewed UI to an app-visible tool in your own server integration.</p><p><a href="/docs/server">Build a validated MCP server integration</a> with complete result schemas, request context, explicit private metadata and standard resource/CSP declarations.</p><p><a href="/docs/reference-workflows">Run five persistent reference workflows</a> with actual MCP tools, reviewed changes and a private local audit.</p><a class="button" href="/components">Explore the catalog</a></article></main><!--$--><!--/$--><footer><div><strong>MCPCN</strong><p>Human control for agentic apps.</p></div><div><a href="/llms.txt">llms.txt</a><a href="https://github.com/alvarovillalbaa/mcpcn-ui">GitHub</a><a href="https://github.com/alvarovillalbaa/mcpcn-ui/blob/main/SECURITY.md">Security</a></div></footer><script src="/_next/static/immutable/chunks/1ddg70z30qn04.js" id="_R_" async=""></script><script>(self.__next_f=self.__next_f||[]).push([0])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"1:\"$Sreact.fragment\"\n2:I[14058,[\"/_next/static/immutable/chunks/29nm6-6cbu5hi.js\",\"/_next/static/immutable/chunks/09nx881wbf89m.js\"],\"\"]\n3:I[43820,[\"/_next/static/immutable/chunks/29nm6-6cbu5hi.js\"],\"default\"]\n4:I[98737,[\"/_next/static/immutable/chunks/29nm6-6cbu5hi.js\"],\"default\"]\n26:I[98025,[\"/_next/static/immutable/chunks/29nm6-6cbu5hi.js\"],\"default\",1]\n:HL[\"/_next/static/immutable/chunks/1wjzvi_w_58jv.css\",\"style\"]\n24:X\n0:{\"P\":null,\"c\":[\"\",\"docs\"],\"q\":\"\",\"i\":false,\"f\":[[[\"\",{\"children\":[\"docs\",{\"children\":[\"__PAGE__\",{},\"$undefined\",\"$undefined\",4608]},\"$undefined\",\"$undefined\",4608]},\"$undefined\",\"$undefined\",4624],[[\"$\",\"$1\",\"c\",{\"children\":[[[\"$\",\"link\",\"0\",{\"rel\":\"stylesheet\",\"href\":\"/_next/static/immutable/chunks/1wjzvi_w_58jv.css\",\"precedence\":\"next\",\"crossOrigin\":\"$undefined\",\"nonce\":\"$undefined\"}],[\"$\",\"script\",\"script-0\",{\"src\":\"/_next/static/immutable/chunks/29nm6-6cbu5hi.js\",\"async\":true,\"nonce\":\"$undefined\"}]],[\"$\",\"html\",null,{\"lang\":\"en\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"body\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"header\",null,{\"className\":\"site-nav\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/\",\"className\":\"brand\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"brand-mark\",\"children\":\"M\"}],\"MCPCN\"]}],[\"$\",\"nav\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L2\",\"/docs\",{\"href\":\"/docs\",\"children\":\"Docs\"}],[\"$\",\"$L2\",\"/components\",{\